    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request was that the \"money owed\" figure on the dashboard should count only invoices that have actually been **sent** \u2014 not drafts, and (as the test confirms) not already-paid ones either.\n\nThe root cause was that the dashboard's outstanding total summed invoices with status `'UNPAID'`, a stale status from before the invoice lifecycle became DRAFT \u2192 SENT \u2192 PAID. That query no longer matched any rows under the current lifecycle.\n\n**Change made** (server-side, the one place the total is computed):\n\n- `InvoiceRepository.java` \u2014 renamed `sumUnpaidAmount()` \u2192 `sumSentAmount()` and changed the JPQL filter to `WHERE i.status = 'SENT'`, so drafts and paid invoices are both excluded.\n- `DashboardGet.java` \u2014 calls the renamed method; updated its doc.\n- `DashboardView.java` and `Dashboard.tsx` \u2014 updated the descriptive comments to match the new semantics.\n\nNo schema migration or front-end behavior change was needed: the `invoice` table already carries `status`, the seed endpoint already accepts it, and the dashboard already renders `data-testid=\"dashboard-outstanding-total\"` through the shared `money()` formatter. With the SENT-only sum, the seeded fixture (100 SENT + 200 SENT, excluding the 50 DRAFT and 30 PAID) yields `$300.00`, and the Playwright spec passes.",
